{
  "abstract": "For infinitely many primes p, Ω(p − 2) is odd, where Ω counts prime factors with multiplicity. We assign nonnegative weights to integers u in [x, 2x] with Ω(u) odd. Using a shifted correlation estimate, we sieve the values u + 2 and obtain a lower bound for the combined weight of primes and products of two large primes. A separate upper bound for the contribution from those products leaves positive weight on primes for every sufficiently large x.\nProof development and Lean formalization by gpt-6 astra.",
